//CELL FILE.. WRITE PULSE: 5ns CURRENT: 40.82uA TRANSISTOR WIDTH: 8.5

-MemCellType: MRAM
-CellArea (F^2): 54
-CellAspectRatio: 0.54
-ResistanceOn (ohm): 3000
-ResistanceOff (ohm): 6000
-ReadMode: current
-ReadVoltage (V): 0.25
-MinSenseVoltage (mV): 25
-ReadPower (uW): 30
-ResetMode: current
-ResetCurrent (uA): 80
-ResetPulse (ns): 10
-ResetEnergy (pJ): 1
-SetMode: current
-SetCurrent (uA): 80
-SetPulse (ns): 10
-SetEnergy (pJ): 1
-AccessType: CMOS
-VoltageDropAccessDevice (V): 0.15
-AccessCMOSWidth (F): 8
# PIMID (1.12.162): write-verify (published STT-MRAM macros program with write-verify-write: Intel 22FFL,
# Wei et al. ISSCC 2019; TSMC 22 nm, Chih et al. ISSCC 2020). From Dong et al., ISSCC 2018
# (28 nm 1 Mb), Fig. 30.2.5a: a 10 ns write fails a bit with probability p = 0.045 (25 C). A round
# re-pulses the failing bits and reads the word back; with independent retries over a 512-bit access
# the expected rounds are sum_k [1 - (1 - p^k)^512] = 2.69, and the pulses per bit 1 / (1 - p) = 1.047.
-WriteVerifyRounds (avg): 2.69
-WritePulsesPerBit (avg): 1.047
# PIMID (1.12.162): the same write when a retry adds to the switching already made, so the chance a bit is still
# unwritten after k rounds is p^(2k-1): rounds 1 + sum_k [1 - (1 - p^(2k-1))^512] = 2.046, pulses per bit
# 1 + sum_k p^(2k-1) = 1.045. Chosen with memory.nvm_write_verify.stt_retries: cumulative.
-CumulativeWriteVerifyRounds (avg): 2.046
-CumulativeWritePulsesPerBit (avg): 1.045
# PIMID (1.12.163): the write supply. STT-MRAM writes need a supply above the logic supply: 1.3 V against a
# 1.15 V read maximum (Intel, US9875783B2); a charge-pumped word line (TSMC 22 nm, ISSCC 2020).
# Pump efficiency 0.5: see RRAM_1T1R.cell.
-WriteSupplyVoltage (V): 1.3
-WritePumpEfficiency (ratio): 0.5
